    "narrative": "The standout play for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Mickey Moniak**, who leads our lineup with a 75.75 efficiency score. He draws a highly favorable matchup against Roki Sasaki; the combination of a +14% park factor and the pitcher's slow delivery\u2014which significantly boosts his stolen base potential\u2014creates an elite environment for production. Similarly, **Isaac Paredes** (68.00) remains a core start against Ure\u00f1a, benefiting from a strong platoon advantage and a premium spot in the #3 hole. While **Corbin Carroll** deals with a tougher SP in Tolle, his speed-centric profile keeps his score at a respectable 60.06, ensuring he remains a priority start despite the challenging matchup.\n\nOur most difficult decision occurred at the corner infield/utility spots, where **Austin Riley** narrowly missed the cut with a 54.83 score. While he presents a solid floor, the optimizer prioritized the higher projected efficiency of **Josh Naylor** (61.02) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (59.32). The decision essentially boiled down to the favorable matchup context for **Josh Naylor** against May, whereas **Austin Riley** was dinged for a lower spot in the batting order. We are also monitoring the status of **Mickey Moniak**, whose score assumes a #6 placement in the lineup; should that official order shift significantly downward, we may see his efficiency score dip closer to our marginal threshold. \n\nWe are avoiding the \"Below Floor\" risks presented by players like **Travis Bazzana** and **Zach McKinstry**, both of whom fall under the 40.00 score threshold due to unfavorable pitcher skill matchups\u2014specifically **Zach McKinstry** drawing the formidable Skenes. Meanwhile, the status of **James Wood** remains unchanged as he continues to occupy an IL slot. We are proceeding with **Brice Turang** and **Henry Bolte** at the top of the order to capitalize on their dynamic speed potential, despite the risks posed by Gilbert and Lugo, respectively. With the scarcity of steals as our primary concern, we are comfortable sacrificing marginal raw point potential in favor of the elite sprint speed assets currently locked into our daily starting nine.",
